\line Troubleshooting / FAQ}
\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql\loch

\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql{\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\fs28\b\loch
I can't get the next mission in a string to trigger.}{\loch
\line \line Try leaving the planet and landing again. The Nova engine is kinda finnicky about multiple missions being offered at the same planet and sometimes an invisible mission triggering will stop further missions from being offered. Sometimes, you'll even have to land on another planet and come back.\line \line Alternatively, there could be a delay for the next mission, there could be a combat rating gate, or it could just be a bug (the developer is only human, after all.) If you strongly suspect it to be the latter, feel free to bug the developer (DrFiveMinusMinus#6697) on discord.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql\loch

\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql{\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\fs28\b\loch
I }{\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\fs28\b\loch
got a strange message when I captured a ship.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql\loch

\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql{\loch
White Dwarf is built around the assumption that you will be flying solo, with your only escorts being fighters of Followers. Capturing escorts will change the balance of combat and will likely make your experience worse. Additionally, large captured escorts will slow down your ship in hyperspace, bypassing the normalized jump times.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql\loch

\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql{\rtlch\afs28\ab \ltrch\loch\fs28\b\loch
I was told to dominate a planet. What does that mean?}
\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql\rtlch\afs24\ab \ltrch\loch\fs24\b\loch

\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql{\rtlch\afs24\ab0 \ltrch\loch\fs24\b0\loch
Planetary Domination is a feature in the EV series that is typically used to allow the player to extort planetary governments for money. In White Dwarf, it is used slightly differently; often appearing as part of the story. To dominate a planet, hail it (by pressing \u8216\'91Y\u8217\'92 after selecting it on your stellar navigation bar using the number keys) and select the \u8220\'93Demand Tribute\u8221\'94 option. The planet should launch its defense fleet, unless it is immune to domination (see below.)}
\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql\rtlch\afs24\ab \ltrch\loch\fs24\b\loch

\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql{\rtlch\afs28\ab \ltrch\loch\fs28\b\loch
I can\u8217\'92t dominate this planet. Why?}
\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql\rtlch\afs28\ab \ltrch\loch\fs28\b\loch

\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql{\rtlch\afs24\ab0 \ltrch\loch\fs24\b0\loch
Not all planets can be dominated in White Dwarf; namely, government capitals and story-relevant planets usually cannot be dominated unless made available by a mission.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql\rtlch\afs24\ab \ltrch\loch\fs24\b\loch

\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql{\rtlch\afs28\ab \ltrch\loch\fs28\b\loch
I don\u8217\'92t remember this in the Nova universe!}
\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql\rtlch\afs24\ab0 \ltrch\loch\fs24\b0\loch

\par \pard\plain \s21\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af0\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f0\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\ql{\rtlch\afs24\ab0 \ltrch\loch\fs24\b0\loch
White Dwarf makes a few lore changes of its own, but most of the new additions to the Nova lore are imported from Brave New Void, my previous work. While you don\u8217\'92t have to have played Brave New Void to understand White Dwarf, those of you who have can assume that everything from BNV is canon in White Dwarf.}
\par }